// Pseudo routing for tenant-aware inference (high level)
function routeRequest(req) {
  const tenant = extractTenant(req);
  const endpoint = getTenantEndpoint(tenant);
  return callModelEndpoint(endpoint, req.payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test canary deployments at scale?
- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding and data deletion?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-preserving ML pipelines across tenants with governance constraints. It also probes how to coordinate training, model registry, and DR while controlling cost.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning across tenants
- Azure ML orchestration and Delta Lake
- Purview RBAC BYOK governance
- Drift monitoring and auditability
- DR and cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for federated training loop
function train_round(tenant_config, local_data_uri, model, aggregator_uri){
  const local_model = train(model, load(local_data_uri));
  const update = compute_update(local_model, model);
  send_update_to_server(aggregator_uri, update);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect and respond to drift across tenants?
- How would you handle non-IID data and stragglers in the federation?
